{
  "abstract": "Complete Lean 4 formalization of the lexicographically sharp all-L^1 Landau-Kolmogorov inequality on any compact interval [a, b] (a < b) and every order n = k + 1 >= 1: ||f^(n)||_1 <= 4^n n! (b-a)^(-n) ||f||_1 + ((b-a)/2) B_n ||f^(n+1)||_1 for f in W^(n+1,1)([a,b]), where B_n = 1 - 2^n/(n+1) + 2^(n+1)/(n+1) sum_{m=1}^{floor((n+1)/2)} (-1)^(m-1) cos^(n+1)(m pi/(n+2)). The development constructs the (n+1)-point moving-node Chebyshev divided- difference operator driven by the eigenvalues of a symmetric tridiagonal Jacobi matrix, proves unconditionally for every n >= 1 that the Peano error profile E_n is strictly decreasing on [0, 1] and attains its unique global maximum on [-1, 1] at t = 0 with value B_n, proves optimality of both constants on C^infty([a,b]), and characterizes equality in C^(n+1)([a,b]) as scalar multiples of the rescaled second-kind Chebyshev polynomial U_n.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Lijails"
    }
